    "narrative": "Our lineup for August 26th is headlined by **Seiya Suzuki**, who commands the highest efficiency score of the day at 75.03. **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a stellar matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez (xERA 4.67) and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery that boosts his stolen base potential, making him a primary target in our pursuit of category scarcity. **Brice Turang** (71.26) and **Corbin Carroll** (70.87) follow closely behind. **Brice Turang** leverages a strong SP skill advantage against Robert Stock, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a core anchor despite facing the lefty Matthew Boyd; his elite speed profile keeps his floor high even when platoon splits aren't perfectly optimal. **Mickey Moniak** is our most surprising riser today with a 67.05 score, driven largely by a massive +14% boost from a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Matt Waldron.\n\nThe bench decision process was particularly tight between **Vinnie Pasquantino** (54.93) and **Griffin Conine** (43.48). While **Griffin Conine** flashed a respectable 0.380 xwOBA, his upside was capped by a tough matchup against Sonny Gray, leaving him on the outside looking in. Conversely, **Vinnie Pasquantino** earns the UTIL start despite a negative SP skill adjustment because his platoon advantage against Spencer Miles is too significant to ignore in a 5x5 format. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood**, who remains on the IL, and we are proceeding with caution given that all scores are currently based on projected lineups. Should official reports shift **Gabriel Moreno** or **Isaac Paredes** out of their anticipated slots, we will re-evaluate our approach to the middle of the order to ensure we aren't chasing empty plate appearances.",
